  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "The tension between former Indonesian Futsal Federation (FFI) Chairman Michael Sianipar and the Football Association of Indonesia (PSSI) escalated following Sianipar's removal from office. Sianipar has formally submitted a complaint to the PSSI Ethics Committee, outlining four primary concerns, including allegations of intervention and denials of his right to respond. While PSSI has confirmed the establishment of an electoral committee and indicated that Sianipar remains eligible to compete in future leadership elections, Sianipar maintains that the upcoming Extraordinary Congress scheduled for December 11 is illegitimate. He has publicly challenged PSSI leadership to provide evidence supporting his dismissal. The situation reflects ongoing administrative friction within the FFI, with PSSI asserting its oversight role while Sianipar continues to contest the procedural validity of the actions taken against his tenure.",
